# No behavior regressions

When changing **game behavior** (movement, combat, targeting, deployment, spells, AI, card rules, grid/pathfinding), do not ship without checking for regressions.

**Reference:** Before changing rules, read the matching logic in `/home/guru/Downloads/clash-royale-main` — see `java-clash-reference.mdc` for the file map.

## Before finishing

1. Run `npm test` in `tiny-wars/` — all tests must pass.
2. Run `npm run build` if types or imports changed.

## When changing behavior

- **Update or add a test** in `src/**/*.test.ts` that would have caught the bug or locks in the new rule.
- Prefer testing pure logic (`LaneMovement`, `Movement`, `EntityGeometry`, `GameSimulator`, etc.) over Phaser scenes.
- If you fix a reported bug (e.g. units stuck at bridge, lost free movement, wrong tower hitbox), add a focused test case for that scenario.

## Existing coverage map

| Area | Test file |
|------|-----------|
| Lane march / bridges | `LaneMovement.test.ts` |
| River / bridge pathing | `Movement.test.ts` |
| Building footprint / surface dist | `EntityGeometry.test.ts`, `Building.test.ts` |
| Deploy rules / sim ticks | `GameSimulator.test.ts` |
| Cards / elixir | `CardSystem.test.ts` |
| Combat helpers | `CombatHelpers.test.ts` |
| Pathfinding | `Pathfinder.test.ts` |

## UI-only changes

Visual tweaks (card layout, sprites, animations) do not require new tests unless they change gameplay input or rules.
